    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain the difference between high glycemic index foods and low glycemic index foods? i'm trying to understand how they affect blood sugar for someone managing type 2 diabetes.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High glycemic index (GI) foods cause a rapid spike in blood sugar because they are digested quickly. Conversely, low GI foods are digested much slower, leading to a gradual and more sustained release of glucose into the bloodstream. For someone with type 2 diabetes, choosing low GI options helps prevent sharp blood sugar peaks and troughs. This steady energy release is much easier for managing blood sugar levels effectively.",
      "source": "target",
