      "content": "When you eat high GI foods, the sugar rapidly enters your bloodstream, signaling your pancreas to release a large amount of insulin quickly. This sudden surge of insulin works hard to move all that sugar out of the blood and into your cells for energy or storage. However, this rapid demand can lead to high blood sugar initially, followed sometimes by a crash as insulin works overtime.",
